<!-- ============================================================ -->
# Introduction # {#introduction}
<!-- ============================================================ -->

*This section is non-normative.*

In [[FEDCM]], when an [=RP=] requests an [=IDP=] whose [[LOGIN-STATUS|login status]] is
[=logged-in=], the [=user agent=] sends a credentialed request to the [=IDP=]'s
{{IdentityProviderAPIConfig/accounts_endpoint}} before the user has chosen an account. That
credentialed fetch enables a timing attack and requires the user agent to show mismatch UI when the
endpoint returns no accounts.

This specification lets an [=IDP=] **push** the user's signed-in accounts to the [=user agent=]
when calling {{NavigatorLogin/setStatus()}}, as described in
[Lightweight FedCM](https://github.com/fedidcg/LightweightFedCM#fedcm-accounts-push):

<div class="example" id="example-push-accounts">
After Alice signs in on `https://idp.example`, the [=IDP=] pushes her account when setting its
login status:

```js
await navigator.login.setStatus("logged-in", {
  accounts: [{
    id: "1234",
    name: "Alice",
    email: "alice@idp.example",
    picture: "https://idp.example/alice.jpg"
  }]
});
```

Because `idp.example` pushes its accounts, its [=config file=] does not need an
{{IdentityProviderAPIConfig/accounts_endpoint}}:

```json
{
  "id_assertion_endpoint": "/assertion",
  "login_url": "/login"
}
```

</div>

This specification is written as a set of monkey patches to [[LOGIN-STATUS]] and [[FEDCM]], shown
like this:

<div class="monkeypatch">
A change to an algorithm or definition in another specification.

</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
# Infrastructure # {#infrastructure}
<!-- ============================================================ -->

This specification depends on the Infra Standard. [[!INFRA]]

<!-- ============================================================ -->
# The Account Registry # {#registry}
<!-- ============================================================ -->

Each [=user agent=] has a global, persistent <dfn>account registry</dfn>, which stores the accounts
that [=IDPs=] push with {{NavigatorLogin/setStatus()}}. It is an initially empty [=map=]. Its
[=map/keys=] are [=/origins=] of [=IDPs=], and its [=map/values=] are
<dfn lt="account registry entry">account registry entries</dfn>. An [=account registry entry=] is
a [=struct=] with the following [=struct/items=]:

<dl dfn-for="account registry entry">
    :   <dfn>accounts</dfn>
    ::  A [=list=] of {{IdentityProviderAccount}}s.
    :   <dfn>expiration</dfn>
    ::  A moment in time, or null for no expiration.
</dl>

<xmp class="idl">
dictionary LoginStatusOptions {
  sequence<IdentityProviderAccount> accounts;
  [EnforceRange] unsigned long long expiration;
};
</xmp>

<dl dfn-type="dict-member" dfn-for="LoginStatusOptions">
    :   <dfn>accounts</dfn>
    ::  The [=list=] of {{IdentityProviderAccount}}s currently signed in at the [=IDP=].
    :   <dfn>expiration</dfn>
    ::  The duration in milliseconds for which the pushed accounts remain valid. If omitted, the
        accounts remain valid until the [=IDP=]'s login status becomes [=logged-out=] or is cleared.
</dl>

<div class="monkeypatch">
In [[LOGIN-STATUS]], change the {{NavigatorLogin/setStatus()}} method so that it takes an optional
second argument, `optional LoginStatusOptions options = {}`, and add the following steps at the
end of its algorithm:

1. If <var ignore>status</var> is `"logged-out"`, [=map/remove=] [=account registry=][|origin|] and return.
1. If |options|["{{LoginStatusOptions/accounts}}"] does not [=map/exist=], return.
1. For each |account| of |options|["{{LoginStatusOptions/accounts}}"]: if |account| has none of
    {{IdentityProviderAccount/name}}, {{IdentityProviderAccount/email}},
    {{IdentityProviderAccount/tel}}, or {{IdentityProviderAccount/username}}, throw a
    {{TypeError}}.
1. Let |expiration| be null.
1. If |options|["{{LoginStatusOptions/expiration}}"] [=map/exists=], set |expiration| to the
    current time plus |options|["{{LoginStatusOptions/expiration}}"] milliseconds.
1. [=map/Set=] [=account registry=][|origin|] to a new struct with
    [=account registry entry/accounts=] |options|["{{LoginStatusOptions/accounts}}"] and
    [=account registry entry/expiration=] |expiration|.

Also, in the algorithm that processes the <code>Set-Login</code> header, when the token is
`"logged-out"`, [=map/remove=] [=account registry=][|origin|].

</div>

<div algorithm>
To <dfn>get the pushed accounts</dfn> for an [=/origin=] |origin|, run the following steps. This
returns a [=list=] of {{IdentityProviderAccount}}s.

1. If [=account registry=][|origin|] does not [=map/exist=], return an empty [=list=].
1. Let |entry| be [=account registry=][|origin|].
1. If |entry|'s [=account registry entry/expiration=] is not null and is in the past,
    [=map/remove=] [=account registry=][|origin|] and return an empty [=list=].
1. If [=get the login status=] for |origin| is not [=logged-in=], return an empty [=list=].
1. Return |entry|'s [=account registry entry/accounts=].

</div>

The user agent MUST clear [=account registry=] entries whenever it clears the corresponding
[=Login Status map=] entries.

<!-- ============================================================ -->
# Presentation # {#presentation}
<!-- ============================================================ -->

This section defines how the [=user agent=] uses the [=account registry=] when presenting accounts
in [[FEDCM]].

<div class="monkeypatch">
In [[FEDCM]], remove the `required` keyword from the
{{IdentityProviderAPIConfig/accounts_endpoint}} member of {{IdentityProviderAPIConfig}}.

In [=fetch the config file=], if
<var ignore>config</var>.{{IdentityProviderAPIConfig/accounts_endpoint}} doesn't [=map/exist=], set
<var ignore>accounts_url</var> to null instead of computing it, and do not treat a null
<var ignore>accounts_url</var> as failure.

Note: An [=IDP=] that pushes its accounts with {{NavigatorLogin/setStatus()}} only needs a
[=config file=] and an {{IdentityProviderAPIConfig/id_assertion_endpoint}}.

</div>

<div class="monkeypatch">
In [=fetch the accounts=], insert the following steps at the beginning of the algorithm:

1. Let |origin| be the [=url/origin=] of the result of running the [=URL parser=] on
    <var ignore>provider</var>'s {{IdentityProviderConfig/configURL}}.
1. Let |pushed| be the result of [=get the pushed accounts=] for |origin|.
1. If |pushed| is not [=list/is empty|empty=], or if
    <var ignore>config</var>["{{IdentityProviderAPIConfig/accounts_endpoint}}"] doesn't
    [=map/exist=], return a new {{IdentityProviderAccountList}} with
    {{IdentityProviderAccountList/accounts}} set to |pushed|.

</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
# Privacy and security considerations # {#privacy-and-security}
<!-- ============================================================ -->

* An [=IDP=] that pushes its accounts and omits
    {{IdentityProviderAPIConfig/accounts_endpoint}} never receives a credentialed request before
    the user selects an account or chooses to sign in. This removes the timing attack that affects
    {{IdentityProviderAPIConfig/accounts_endpoint}}.
* The [=account registry=] is global to the [=user agent=], is used only in user agent UI, and is
    never exposed to the [=RP=] until the user selects an account.
* Entries in the [=account registry=] are scoped to the [=IDP=]'s [=/origin=], expire when
    {{LoginStatusOptions/expiration}} elapses, and are cleared whenever the [=IDP=] sets its login
    status to [=logged-out=] or the user clears browsing data for that [=/origin=].
